@startuml FRQ-PRC-16.3-capture-sequence
' Prolaz prihvata kako ga stvarno vodi temeljni procesor.
' Gledište: izvedba. Publika: implementator, tester.
' Prikaz, ne izvor istine (D-13) — izvor su concrete/processor.py (GenericProcessor.start),
' kod blackwattle processors/sdr.py (usklađeno 2026-09-11) i FRQ-PRC-16.3 §5–§6.
' Crveno: mjesta gdje se zatečeni ugovor razilazi s FRQ-PRC-16.3 — nalazi, ne odluke.
title FRQ-PRC-16.3 — capture pass as the base processor runs it

autonumber
skinparam SequenceMessageAlignment center

participant "caller" as C
participant "p :\nSDRReadProcessor\n(start: base)" as P
participant "p :\nSDRReadProcessor\n(create_generator)" as G
participant "drv :\nDriverSDR" as DRV
participant "bb :\nBlackboard" as BB
participant "pl :\nPipeline" as PL

C -> P : start()
activate P
P -> P : blackboard present, ≥ 1 pipeline (base check)
P -> G : create_generator()
activate G
G -> DRV : ensure_live() — unit claimed before the first document (BR-06)
G -> DRV : read(uri)
note right of DRV : the schedule — one frequency or the\ntuning plan — belongs to the connection
loop blocks until the boundary: stop_blocks or stop_seconds (BR-08)
  alt the block changes frequency, or the segment is full
    G -> BB : create(caller=p, content=segment samples,\nmetadata=description + counts)
    BB --> G : item
    G --> P : yield item
    P -> PL : process(processor=p, item)
    alt a pipeline raises
      PL --> P : PipelineException
      note right of P #FFCDD2
        Rule (author, 2026-09-11): a pipeline failure
        ends the pass. The suspended generator closes
        later and records the pass as partial.
      end note
    else every pipeline succeeds
      P -> BB : flush(caller=p, **write_context)
      P -> P : INFO Processed (base: one record per document)
    end
  end
end
alt boundary reached
  G -> DRV : close the block generator — the session ends
  G -> G : INFO Finished: summary once per pass
else device lost (BR-09)
  DRV --> G : SDRDeviceLost
  G -> G : WARNING Finished: summary marked partial
  G --> P : ProcessorException
end
deactivate G
P -> P : INFO Completed (cycles)
deactivate P

note over P, PL #FFCDD2
  The base loop writes one INFO per document and the processor one summary
  per pass: with small segments the INFO stream grows with the capture
  (FRQ-PRC-16.3 §11 t.5).
end note
@enduml
